       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **A different dose or drug**, if 30 mg was a typo or you were thinking of another medication.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note saying the dose is intentional and above the labeled maximum. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
      }
